  "design": {
    "training": "640 examples balanced to 80 per category. This split contains 197 reviewed v0.2 training examples, 50 former v0.2 validation examples after diagnosis-label normalization, and 393 new or replacement synthetic cases.",
    "validation": "128 newly authored prompts, 16 per category, with unique IDs and input payloads. Some underlying repair patterns recur across splits as required to measure the same fixed diagnosis taxonomy.",
    "evaluation": "192 newly authored held-out prompts, 24 per category and four per canonical diagnosis code. The prompts have unique case IDs, input data and execution descriptions and are excluded from training. Some underlying repair patterns recur because the diagnosis taxonomy is finite; this remains a synthetic controlled benchmark.",
    "diagnosis_codes": "48 canonical labels, six per category. The Colab pipeline adds concise definitions for all codes to the shared system instruction at runtime, identically across training, validation and evaluation.",
    "retrieval": "The same official-document BM25 retrieval and augmentation policy is used for training, validation and evaluation. The same runtime system instruction includes concise canonical-code definitions.",
    "safety": "Credentials and secrets always abstain. External outages and ambiguous item lineage abstain unless supplied evidence supports a safe, minimal correction.",
    "limits": "Synthetic benchmark; not representative of all real n8n failures. Patch applicability checks the JSON fixture and workflow graph only; it does not execute n8n. A gold-patch match is strict and may penalize alternative valid repairs.",
    "item_linking": "A missing paired-item link may be repaired with .first() only when the prompt explicitly guarantees exactly one upstream item; otherwise it must abstain and request human review."
  },
  "validation": "128 newly authored cases, 16 per category, separate from training.",
